{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 0,
    "dDurationMs": 4259,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is a moment that almost every married couple in this country will face, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4259,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the tax code is waiting for it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6160,
    "dDurationMs": 5599,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The day one spouse dies, the surviving one becomes poorer almost overnight, and then the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11759,
    "dDurationMs": 3221,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "federal government does something that feels impossible to believe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15179,
    "dDurationMs": 1322,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It raises their taxes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17001,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Less income coming in, and a bigger share of it going out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20800,
    "dDurationMs": 3381,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It has a name among the few advisers who are honest about it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24341,
    "dDurationMs": 5279,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They call it the widow's penalty, and it quietly takes tens of thousands of dollars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29620,
    "dDurationMs": 6181,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from grieving spouses every single year, mostly women, because women tend to outlive their husbands."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36320,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Almost nobody is warned about it until the first tax return comes due and the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41240,
    "dDurationMs": 2180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "number on the page makes no sense."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43600,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I want to walk you through exactly how this trap works, because once you see"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48140,
    "dDurationMs": 5601,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the machinery you can disarm it, but only while both spouses are still alive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54362,
    "dDurationMs": 4199,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Everything I am about to show you has to be done before the funeral, not"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58561,
    "dDurationMs": 2341,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "after. After, the door is closed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61381,
    "dDurationMs": 3980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I am going to give you the seven moving parts of the widow's penalty and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65361,
    "dDurationMs": 2321,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then the moves that protect against each one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68081,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Stay with me to the end, because the last move is the one that saves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71641,
    "dDurationMs": 3461,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the most money and the one the fewest people ever make."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75262,
    "dDurationMs": 4359,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let me start with the engine that drives the whole thing, and it is something"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79621,
    "dDurationMs": 2562,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "most people have never thought about."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82183,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The I R S decides your filing status by where you stand on the thirty"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87483,
    "dDurationMs": 979,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "first of December."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88683,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For the year your spouse actually passes away, you are still allowed to file married"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93903,
    "dDurationMs": 2679,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "filing jointly one final time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96822,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the very next year, you file as a single person."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100162,
    "dDurationMs": 6021,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is one narrow exception called qualifying surviving spouse that lets you keep the married"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106183,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rates for two more years, and it only applies if you have a dependent child"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110563,
    "dDurationMs": 860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "living in your home."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111423,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For the vast majority of seniors whose children are grown and gone, that exception does"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116343,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not exist. So one year you are taxed as a couple, and the next year,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120784,
    "dDurationMs": 4339,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while you are still grieving, you are taxed as a single person on almost the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125123,
    "dDurationMs": 4301,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "same income. That single switch is what sets off everything that follows."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129743,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number one is the bracket collapse, and this is the heart of the trap."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134544,
    "dDurationMs": 4940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The tax brackets for a married couple are exactly twice as wide as the brackets"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139484,
    "dDurationMs": 1160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for a single person."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140954,
    "dDurationMs": 5050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In twenty twenty six, a married couple stays in the twelve percent bracket all the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146004,
    "dDurationMs": 7701,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "way up to ninety six thousand nine hundred and fifty dollars of taxable income."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153705,
    "dDurationMs": 3579,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A single person crosses out of twelve percent and into twenty two percent at just"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157284,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "forty eight thousand four hundred and seventy five dollars, less than half as far."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163145,
    "dDurationMs": 4679,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the moment a survivor files single, income that used to be taxed at twelve"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167824,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "percent gets taxed at twenty two percent, even though not a single thing about that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173064,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "income has changed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174405,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The brackets did not move."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176405,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The person simply lost the spouse who doubled the width of every one of them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180765,
    "dDurationMs": 3321,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number two is the standard deduction getting cut almost in half."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184506,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In twenty twenty six a married couple filing jointly gets a standard deduction of thirty"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188956,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "two thousand two hundred dollars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191716,
    "dDurationMs": 3889,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A single person gets sixteen thousand one hundred dollars, exactly half."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195605,
    "dDurationMs": 4741,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is still a small additional deduction for being sixty five or older, and there"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200346,
    "dDurationMs": 4419,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is still the new senior bonus deduction of up to six thousand dollars that runs"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204765,
    "dDurationMs": 2241,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through twenty twenty eight, and those help."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 207545,
    "dDurationMs": 4781,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the core deduction that shields your income from tax shrinks by half the year"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 212326,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the survivor files alone."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214287,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Less shield, narrower brackets, same income."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217706,
    "dDurationMs": 1660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can already see where this is going."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219766,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number three is the one that feels the cruelest, because it is the income actually"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224146,
    "dDurationMs": 5301,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "going down. When one spouse dies, Social Security does not keep paying both checks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229947,
    "dDurationMs": 5039,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The survivor keeps the larger of the two benefits and the smaller one stops completely."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 235206,
    "dDurationMs": 3581,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if one of you was collecting two thousand dollars a month and the other"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 238787,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was collecting fourteen hundred, the survivor does not get thirty four hundred anymore."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243907,
    "dDurationMs": 1821,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The survivor gets two thousand."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246108,
    "dDurationMs": 5620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That fourteen hundred dollar check is simply gone, which can be fifteen or sixteen thousand"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251728,
    "dDurationMs": 5019,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dollars a year vanishing from the household at the exact moment everything else is getting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256747,
    "dDurationMs": 1661,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more expensive to face alone."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258567,
    "dDurationMs": 5281,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number four is that more of the Social Security that remains becomes taxable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264028,
    "dDurationMs": 6219,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whether your Social Security is taxed depends on something called provisional income, and here is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 270247,
    "dDurationMs": 2361,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the quiet unfairness built into it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 272687,
    "dDurationMs": 5312,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For a married couple, the income thresholds where Social Security starts getting taxed are thirty"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277999,
    "dDurationMs": 3669,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "two thousand and forty four thousand dollars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 281668,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For a single person, those same thresholds drop to twenty five thousand and thirty four"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 286468,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thousand. They are lower for one person than they were for two."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 290468,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the survivor, living on less money, often finds that a larger percentage of her"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 295468,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Social Security is now exposed to tax than when there were two people and two"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 300548,
    "dDurationMs": 920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "checks in the house."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301668,
    "dDurationMs": 6361,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number five is the required minimum distribution crossfire, and this one catches people who think"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 308029,
    "dDurationMs": 2740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they can simply spend less to stay safe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311490,
    "dDurationMs": 3719,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Starting at age seventy three, the I R S forces you to pull a minimum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315209,
    "dDurationMs": 4341,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "amount out of every traditional I R A and four oh one k you own,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 319870,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whether you need the money or not."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 322329,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That forced withdrawal counts as taxable income no matter what you do with it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326949,
    "dDurationMs": 5961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While both spouses were alive, that distribution was absorbed inside the wide married brackets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 332910,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After one spouse dies, the very same withdrawal, often on a very similar account balance,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 339290,
    "dDurationMs": 3661,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gets pushed up into the narrower single brackets and taxed harder."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343531,
    "dDurationMs": 1759,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The survivor cannot turn it off."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 345730,
    "dDurationMs": 3681,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The law requires the money to come out, and the law requires it to be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 349411,
    "dDurationMs": 1199,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "taxed at the single rate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 350850,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number six is the Medicare surcharge, and most people do not even know it is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 355310,
    "dDurationMs": 6740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hiding here. It is called I R M A A, the income related monthly adjustment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 362050,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "amount, and it is an extra charge added to your Medicare premiums once your income"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 367550,
    "dDurationMs": 1421,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "passes a certain line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 369151,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And just like everything else, the line for a single person is half of the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373451,
    "dDurationMs": 880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "line for a couple."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374632,
    "dDurationMs": 5069,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In twenty twenty six the surcharge starts at around two hundred and eighteen thousand dollars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 379701,
    "dDurationMs": 6700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of income for a married couple, but only around one hundred and nine thousand for"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 386401,
    "dDurationMs": 151,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a single person."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 386552,
    "dDurationMs": 4599,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A survivor whose income looks modest as half of a couple can suddenly find herself"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 391151,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over the single line, paying hundreds or even thousands of dollars a year in higher"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 396031,
    "dDurationMs": 5781,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Medicare premiums. And because Medicare looks at your tax return from two years earlier, the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 401812,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bill often arrives long after the loss, when she has no idea what triggered it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 406312,
    "dDurationMs": 961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So there it is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 407473,
    "dDurationMs": 2139,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The filing status flips to single."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 409932,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The brackets collapse to half their width."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 412533,
    "dDurationMs": 2079,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The standard deduction is cut in half."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414952,
    "dDurationMs": 2060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One Social Security check disappears."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 417512,
    "dDurationMs": 2581,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "More of the remaining check gets taxed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 420192,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The forced retirement withdrawals get taxed harder."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423512,
    "dDurationMs": 3721,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the Medicare surcharge waits at a line set half as high."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 427612,
    "dDurationMs": 4621,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Six blades, and they all fall at once, on the person least equipped at that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 432233,
    "dDurationMs": 1259,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "moment to fight back."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 433492,
    "dDurationMs": 4642,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is the widow's penalty, and now you know why the tax bill makes no"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 438134,
    "dDurationMs": 3039,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sense to the person sitting at the kitchen table holding it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 441194,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now let me give you the part nobody puts in the title, which is what"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445134,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you actually do about it, because the tax code that built this trap also contains"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 450574,
    "dDurationMs": 1219,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every escape hatch."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 452334,
    "dDurationMs": 4639,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The work has to happen while both spouses are alive and both are healthy enough"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456973,
    "dDurationMs": 1940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to sign documents and make changes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 458913,
    "dDurationMs": 2620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here is where the real money is saved."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 462053,
    "dDurationMs": 4167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The most powerful move is to slowly convert money out of your traditional I R"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 466220,
    "dDurationMs": 4375,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A and into a Roth I R A during the years you are still married"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 470595,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and still filing jointly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 472555,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is move number seven, and it is the one most people never make."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 476875,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While you are a couple, you can move money out of that traditional account and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 481035,
    "dDurationMs": 4919,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fill up those wide twelve percent and twenty two percent married brackets at a known,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 485954,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reasonable tax rate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 487334,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You pay the tax now, while the brackets are wide, and that money becomes a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 492074,
    "dDurationMs": 2021,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Roth account that is never taxed again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 494334,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are no forced withdrawals from a Roth, the growth is tax free, and when"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 498954,
    "dDurationMs": 5021,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one spouse passes, the survivor inherits an account she can draw from without it adding"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 503975,
    "dDurationMs": 5621,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a single dollar to her taxable income or pushing her toward that Medicare surcharge."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 510016,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You are taking a lifetime of future taxes that would have landed on a grieving"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 514296,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "single filer and paying a smaller, controlled amount now while there are still two of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 519816,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you to share the wide brackets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 521916,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This takes several years to do well, which is exactly why you cannot wait."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 526556,
    "dDurationMs": 4839,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The second protective move is about your regular brokerage account and how it is titled,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 531395,
    "dDurationMs": 2961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because of something called the step up in basis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 535017,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When a spouse dies, the investments the survivor inherits get their cost reset to whatever"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 540897,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they are worth on the day of death, and all the built up gain before"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 545017,
    "dDurationMs": 2739,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that simply disappears for tax purposes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 548596,
    "dDurationMs": 4461,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A stock or a fund that was bought decades ago for very little can be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 553057,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "inherited and sold the next day with little or no capital gains tax at all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 558116,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this only works if the account is titled correctly for your state, and the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 562976,
    "dDurationMs": 4001,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rules are different in community property states than in the rest of the country."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 566977,
    "dDurationMs": 5141,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is worth one conversation with an estate attorney to make sure your accounts are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 572118,
    "dDurationMs": 4439,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "set up to capture the full step up, because the wrong titling can cost the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 576557,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "survivor tens of thousands of dollars she never needed to pay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 580817,
    "dDurationMs": 3581,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The third protective move is your pension, if you have one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 584798,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Many pensions default to paying a larger check while the worker is alive and then"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 589518,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stopping completely when that person dies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 592038,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is almost always an option to take a somewhat smaller monthly check in exchange"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 597438,
    "dDurationMs": 4281,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the pension continuing to pay the surviving spouse for the rest of her life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 602259,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That choice is usually locked in at the moment you start drawing the pension, so"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 606599,
    "dDurationMs": 3599,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it has to be considered before you retire, not after."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 610438,
    "dDurationMs": 4921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you are already locked into the single life option, a properly sized life insurance"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 615359,
    "dDurationMs": 5839,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "policy can sometimes replace that lost income for the survivor, but that too requires both"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 621198,
    "dDurationMs": 4921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spouses to be healthy enough to qualify, which again means now and not later."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 626379,
    "dDurationMs": 4221,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the fourth protective move is the simplest one and the one people forget."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 630879,
    "dDurationMs": 6780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Check the beneficiary designations on every retirement account, every life insurance policy, and every bank"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 637659,
    "dDurationMs": 4541,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "account, and make sure each one names the person you intend, and consider naming a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 642200,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "backup beneficiary as well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 643720,
    "dDurationMs": 2459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These forms override whatever your will says."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 646179,
    "dDurationMs": 4181,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "An out of date beneficiary form is one of the most common and most expensive"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 650360,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mistakes in this entire area, and fixing it costs nothing but a few minutes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 654740,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let me tie it together, because the thread running through all of this is the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 659860,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "same one that runs through everything the system does to seniors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 663760,
    "dDurationMs": 4061,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The widow's penalty is not an accident and it is not a secret, it has"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 667821,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "been documented for forty years, and yet no one whose job touches your money has"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 672821,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "any reason to bring it up before it is too late."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 675461,
    "dDurationMs": 1580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Your bank will not mention it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 677160,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most generic financial advisers will not model it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 680020,
    "dDurationMs": 2401,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The I R S certainly will not warn you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 682480,
    "dDurationMs": 4701,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It simply waits, quietly, for the day the household goes from two people to one,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 687181,
    "dDurationMs": 1719,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then it collects."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 689721,
    "dDurationMs": 4941,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But every single one of these traps can be softened or removed entirely with planning"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 694662,
    "dDurationMs": 5020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "done while both spouses are still here, still well, and still able to act together."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 700442,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The couples who sit down and do this work protect the one who will be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 703562,
    "dDurationMs": 4159,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "left behind. The couples who never get around to it leave that person to face"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 707721,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "six tax traps alone, in the worst year of her life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 711221,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you are married, the most loving financial thing you can do is to model"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 715881,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what your taxes will look like the year after one of you is gone, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 719841,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then take the steps to protect whoever that survivor will be."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 723361,
    "dDurationMs": 5522,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Find a fee only fiduciary adviser or an estate planning attorney who understands the widow's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 728883,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "penalty, and bring them these seven points."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 731363,
    "dDurationMs": 3979,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I will put all the details and the things to ask about in the description"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 735342,
    "dDurationMs": 2521,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "below. So do one thing for me right now."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 738283,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Send this to one married couple you care about, while both of them are still"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 742383,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "here to do something about it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 744342,
    "dDurationMs": 5260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Your parents, your sister and her husband, the couple next door, the two people at"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 749602,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "church who have been together fifty years and assume the system will treat the survivor"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 753962,
    "dDurationMs": 1961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "kindly. It will not."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 756503,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One quiet conversation tonight, between two people who still have time, can save the one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 762303,
    "dDurationMs": 5140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who is left behind tens of thousands of dollars and a cruel surprise in the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 767443,
    "dDurationMs": 1681,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hardest year they will ever face."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 769644,
    "dDurationMs": 1559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is what we are here for."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 771764,
    "dDurationMs": 1419,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I will see you in the next one."
    } ]
  } ]
}
